<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thondaiman dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1686–<a href="/years/1948">1948</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thondaiman dynasty ruled Pudukkottai in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a> from the late 17th century until the state joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1948. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghunatha-raya-thondaiman">Raghunatha Raya Thondaiman</a> founded the principality around 1686, and the family's support for the British in the Carnatic wars kept it independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> and Ramnad. Pudukkottai was the only princely state of the Tamil country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thondaiman-dynasty.jpg" alt="Thondaiman dynasty" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Linnaeus Tripe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Todiman_Raja_in_his_Durbar,_Pudukkottai,_1858.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
